load @term/seed/theory/lattice
  find lattice

# A Boolean algebra: a lattice with a top and bottom and a complement for every element, the algebra of classical truth
# (and, or, not) and of subsets (intersection, union, complement). Every Boolean algebra is the algebra of clopen sets
# of a space (Stone's theorem). It is the two-valued logic the surface checker decides in. The form carries the
# underlying lattice; the top, bottom, and complement are the added structure.
form boolean-algebra
  link lattice, like lattice
